Runs an MC simulation for a solute in TIP4P water
to compute heats and volumes of solution.

The solute Z-matrix needs to be in the molecules/OPLS2020 directory.
An equilibration of 25M is followed by 500M or 5000M (5B)  averaging. 
The solvent is 500 TIP4P water molecules with 10-A cutoffs at 25 C, 1 atm.

The mc500par1 and mc500par3 files are setup assuming that atom 1 or 3 is the center
atom of the solute. They can be modified if, for example, specific rdfs are desired. 

xMC5001 executes 500M in the current window. Center atom of solute is atom 1. 
xMC5003 executes 500M in the current window. Center atom of solute is atom 3. 
xMC500Q1 executes 500M in the queueing system. Center atom of solute is atom 1.
xMC500Q3 executes 500M in the queueing system. Center atom of solute is atom 3.
xMC5bQ1 executes 5B in the queueing system. Center atom of solute is atom 1. 
xMC5bQ3 executes 5B in the queueing system. Center atom of solute is atom 3. 

Sample output is provided in the butane, butane5b, and phenol directories. 
This came from executing:
xMC500Q1 butane
xMC5bQ1  butane
xMC500Q3 phenol

Results for many molecules generated with 5B averaging are in
PCCP, 2024, 26, 8141-8147. 
